#: ../../../reference/interfaces/system-backup-interface.md:2
msgid "system-backup interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/system-backup-interface.md:4
msgid ""
"`system-backup` provides read-only access to the system via `/var/lib/snapd/"
"hostfs`. This interface gives privileged access to system data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/system-backup-interface.md:6
msgid "**Auto-connect**: no **Transitional**: no"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/system-backup-interface.md:9
msgid "Requires snapd version _2.43+_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/system-backup-interface.md:11
msgid ""
"By design, snaps using `strict` and `devmode` {ref}`confinement <explanation-"
"security-snap-confinement>` run with a different root filesystem than the "
"host. Snaps that implement a backup function, however, need access to the "
"host's snap-related files outside of this confinement, and this is where the "
"`system-backup` interface can help."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/system-backup-interface.md:13
msgid ""
"The system-backup interface provides read-only access to files under the "
"following location:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/system-backup-interface.md:15
msgid "`/var/lib/snapd/hostfs`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/system-backup-interface.md:17
msgid "With the following exceptions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/system-backup-interface.md:18
msgid "`/var/lib/snapd/hostfs/dev`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/system-backup-interface.md:19
msgid "`/var/lib/snapd/hostfs/proc`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/system-backup-interface.md:20
msgid "`/var/lib/snapd/hostfs/sys`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/system-backup-interface.md:22
msgid ""
"Importantly, neither snapd nor this interface provide any mechanisms to "
"ensure the system is in a ready state for backups. Reliable backup "
"strategies with snaps utilising this interface will need to account for this "
"themselves."
msgstr ""
